-- title:
--   Smooth fibres in characteristic ℓ ∤ N of the integral model
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N$ with $N \neq 0$ and a natural number $\ell$ that is prime, and assume $\ell \nmid N$. Let $F$ be the field `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, namely the subfield of the Laurent series field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the set of expansions $\{\,\mathrm{qExpand}\;\mathbb{Q}\;d\;j_q : d \mid N,\ d \neq 0\,\}$, and let $j =$ `jFull N` be the element $j_q$ of $F$. Over $\mathbb{Z}$ one forms the two-chart integral model [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel ℤ F j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236): the pushout in schemes of the two morphisms `fFin`, `fInf` from the middle chart to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $F$ generated by $j$ and to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$, and `toBase` is the morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Z}$ obtained by descending the two structure morphisms along the pushout. Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $\ell$. The assertion is that the second projection of the pullback of `toBase` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $\mathbb{Z} \to k$, that is the base-changed morphism $\mathcal{X}_{\mathbb{Z}} \times_{\operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Z}} \operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} k$, is smooth of relative dimension $1$.
--
--   This is Igusa's good-reduction statement for the modular curve of level $N$, read on the two-chart model over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$: away from $N$ the fibres are smooth curves. It feeds the construction of the smooth models used further on, being cited by [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.smooth_pullback_snd_toBase_int_of_isUnit_natCast`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.smooth_pullback_snd_toBase_int_of_isUnit_natCast), [`ModularCurve.exists_dRModelPackage_ffPin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_dRModelPackage_ffPin) and [`ModularCurve.nonempty_legTwoInputV2`](thm.html#ModularCurve.nonempty_legTwoInputV2).
